                <p>

                    Mathematics is offered from
                    Grade 8 through Grade 12,
                    including Grade 12 upgrading.

                    Physics is offered from
                    Grade 10 through Grade 12,
                    including Grade 12 upgrading.

                </p>

            </details>


            <details>

                <summary>
                    Are lessons online or face-to-face?
                </summary>

                <p>

                    Both options are offered.

                    Online lessons use Zoom,
                    while face-to-face tuition is
                    available in Newcastle,
                    subject to the programme
                    and availability.

                </p>

            </details>


            <details>

                <summary>
                    Which curricula are supported?
                </summary>

                <p>

                    The existing centre states that
                    lessons support NSC, IEB and SACAI
                    learners and are aligned with the
                    relevant Annual Teaching Plan.

                </p>

            </details>


            <details>

                <summary>
                    How does registration work?
                </summary>

                <p>

                    Start with an enquiry.

                    The centre can confirm the learner's
                    programme, availability, fees and
                    registration requirements before
                    you proceed.

                </p>

            </details>


            <details>

                <summary>
                    Can learners receive individual support?
                </summary>

                <p>

                    Yes.

                    PhysiMaths offers individual,
                    duplet and quartet tuition options,
                    alongside group tuition.

                </p>

            </details>

        </div>

